{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Eastward.</b> Its meaning is from the east. Know that everything we find written is true and so it was, and there is no doubt in it — and it has a sod. For from the light of the intellect, desire went forth, and from the second, that which ascends above, for the movement of desire inward — he also wrapped himself in a fig leaf as a sign, and the third is called by the name of discernment, for at first there is power without an agent, and the one who understands this sod will understand how the river divides, and this is the sod of the Garden of Eden, and 'garments of skin' also indicates this sod, that there is a capacity in man that he be forever, and the discerning will understand that this is the whole of man:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is highly compressed and at points elliptical; rendered hyper-literally throughout without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:07.053233063Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}